A||||7||BlackDragon||how do you turn a notchback to a fastback?||||1||
Z||000000||BlackDragon||08-20-2001||09:41 PM||||what parts are needed, how hard is it? how much time is involved? does it work right, or should i just buy a notchback? any information would be nice||||reg||1
Z||000001||gt boy||08-20-2001||09:54 PM||||you need a bunch of parts..you are best to by a complete car that has the whole rear clip,taillights..etc.  this way you have everything.<P>the trick thought is to find one that is in rough shape that you can get real cheap instead of finding all the parts you need individually as it can be much more expensive that way.<P>i have just one of those types of cars that i am trying to sell at the moment ..a complete 86 gt that has a blown motor..it would be a perfect car for someone like you ready to do the conversion.  too bad you live so far away or we could do a deal.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||08-20-2001||11:00 PM||||You can actually do the conversion in a weekend if you have all the parts. I have seen the parts needed to do this for as low as $200 and up to $600+...<P>I was gonna convert one of mine but I think I'm just gonna leave it a nothcback. I already have a fastback GT anyway...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever3000||08-20-2001||11:29 PM||||A lot of peeps like the notchback better, but if you're serious...<BR>  <A HREF="http://msnhomepages.talkcity.com/RallyRd/scca_fiero/converting2fastback.html" TARGET=_blank>http://msnhomepages.talkcity.com/RallyRd/scca_fiero/converting2fastback.html</A> <BR>...<BR>and<BR>... <A HREF="http://www.fiero.net/showroom/fastback.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.net/showroom/fastback.html</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever3000 (edited 08-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||mbramble||08-21-2001||07:43 AM||||Don't do it -- leave it a notchback!!!, especially if it already has the aero package.  The Indy, 85 GT, and 86/87 SE are the best looking body styles -- IMHO...||||reg||1
Z||000005||Songman||08-21-2001||12:33 PM||||I plan to use Aus's notchback extensions on my clone whenever he gets them ready... also going to try to do the updated quarter window area like in the picture...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AUSindypace2a.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||14
Z||000006||skitime||08-21-2001||02:53 PM||||I visited with JimmyBPEI in Prince Edward Island on our vacation in Canada. He had done and awesome mod to his notchback. He installed GT taillights on a notchback and modified the rear quarter panels and original trunk lid to make it work. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P8140026.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||BlackDragon||08-22-2001||08:34 PM||||decided to just keep the notch, and buy a fast. thanx for the input||||reg||1
